Review written to `docs/reviews/cross-cutting/xcut-02-fuel-type-enum-consistency.md`.

**Summary of findings (5 total):**

| Severity | Finding |
|----------|---------|
| Critical | Unrecognized HPXML fuel strings silently default to `Electric` (e.g. "district heating", "solar", "biogas" → treated as zero-emission) |
| Medium   | `"none"` maps to `Electric` in HPXML parsers but to `None` in the equipment helper — inconsistent across code paths |
| Medium   | Observer `capture_ports()`/`diff_ports()` omit Wood, Coal, WoodPellet despite full enum/parser/equipment support |
| Low      | Generator hardcodes `FuelType::Gas` regardless of HPXML `<FuelType>` config |
| Low      | `FuelAccumulator` Electric slot (index 0) is allocated but never populated (electric flows through `ElectricalAccumulator` instead) |

**Verified correct:** HPXML string round-trip, dual-fuel port contributions (no double-counting), grid-vs-solar handled at `ElectricalAccumulator` level, Btu/therm↔Joule conversions use precise NIST values.
